{"id":"mahabharata-4-022","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":22,"title":"द्वाविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 22 · Bhima kills the Upakichakas","summary":{"en":"Kichaka's kinsmen, the Upakichakas, find the mangled body and, blaming the sairandhri, bind her to be burned with him. Draupadi cries out the secret names of her husbands; Bhima, hearing her, uproots a tree, kills all hundred and five of them, and frees her, to the amazement of the townsfolk.","kn":"ಕೀಚಕನ ಬಂಧುಗಳಾದ ಉಪಕೀಚಕರು ನುಜ್ಜುಗುಜ್ಜಾದ ದೇಹವನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಸೈರಂಧ್ರಿಯನ್ನು ದೂಷಿಸಿ ಅವನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸುಡಲು ಅವಳನ್ನು ಕಟ್ಟುತ್ತಾರೆ. ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಪತಿಗಳ ರಹಸ್ಯ ಹೆಸರುಗಳನ್ನು ಕೂಗುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ಅದನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿದ ಭೀಮನು ಮರ ಕಿತ್ತು ನೂರೈದು ಮಂದಿಯನ್ನೂ ಕೊಂದು ಅವಳನ್ನು ಬಿಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಪುರಜನರು ಬೆರಗಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"कीचक के बन्धु उपकीचक कुचला हुआ शव पाकर सैरन्ध्री को दोषी ठहराते हैं और उसे कीचक के साथ जलाने के लिए बाँध देते हैं। द्रौपदी अपने पतियों के गुप्त नाम पुकारती हैं; यह सुनकर भीम एक वृक्ष उखाड़कर उन सभी एक सौ पाँच को मार डालते हैं और उन्हें मुक्त करते हैं, जिससे पुरवासी चकित रह जाते हैं।","te":"కీచకుని బంధువులైన ఉపకీచకులు నలిగిన శరీరాన్ని చూసి సైరంధ్రిని నిందించి అతనితో కాల్చడానికి ఆమెను కట్టివేస్తారు. ద్రౌపది భర్తల రహస్య నామాలను పిలుస్తుంది; అది విన్న భీముడు చెట్టు పెకలించి నూట ఐదుగురినీ చంపి ఆమెను విడిపిస్తాడు, పౌరులు ఆశ్చర్యపోతారు.","ta":"கீசகனின் உறவினர்களான உபகீசகர்கள் நசுங்கிய உடலைக் கண்டு ஸைரந்த்ரியைக் குற்றம் சாட்டி அவனுடன் எரிக்க அவளைக் கட்டுகிறார்கள். திரௌபதி தன் கணவர்களின் ரகசியப் பெயர்களைக் கூவ, அதைக் கேட்ட பீமன் ஒரு மரத்தைப் பிடுங்கி நூற்றைந்து பேரையும் கொன்று அவளை விடுவிக்க, நகர மக்கள் வியக்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"കീചകന്റെ ബന്ധുക്കളായ ഉപകീചകർ ചതഞ്ഞരഞ്ഞ ശരീരം കണ്ട്, സൈരന്ധ്രിയെ കുറ്റപ്പെടുത്തി അവളെയും അവനോടൊപ്പം ദഹിപ്പിക്കാൻ കെട്ടിയിടുന്നു. ദ്രൗപദി ഭർത്താക്കന്മാരുടെ രഹസ്യനാമങ്ങൾ വിളിച്ചുകരയുന്നു; അത് കേട്ട ഭീമൻ ഒരു മരം പിഴുത് നൂറ്റഞ്ചു ഉപകീചകരെയും കൊന്ന്, അവളെ മോചിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. നഗരവാസികൾ അത്ഭുതപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.22; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"कीचकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Kichakavadha Parva (Slaying of Kichaka)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मिन्काले समागम्य सर्वे तत्रास्य बान्धवाः ।\nरुरुदुः कीचकं दृष्ट्वा परिवार्य समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that time all his kinsmen gathered there and wept, crowding around Kichaka."}},{"n":2,"text":"सर्वे संहृष्टरोमाणः संत्रस्ताः प्रेक्ष्य कीचकम् ।\nतथा सर्वाङ्गसंभुग्नं कूर्मं स्थल इवोद्धृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All were seized with horror and fear on seeing Kichaka, broken in every limb like a tortoise dragged onto land."}},{"n":3,"text":"पोथितं भीमसेनेन तमिन्द्रेणेव दानवम् ।\nसंस्कारयितुमिच्छन्तो बहिर्नेतुं प्रचक्रमुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had been crushed by Bhimasena as Indra crushed a danava; wishing to perform his funeral, they began to carry him outside."}},{"n":4,"text":"ददृशुस्ते ततः कृष्णां सूतपुत्राः समागताः ।\nअदूरादनवद्याङ्गीं स्तम्भमालिङ्ग्य तिष्ठतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the charioteers who had assembled saw Krishna, blameless in body, standing not far off, clinging to a pillar."}},{"n":5,"text":"समवेतेषु सूतेषु तानुवाचोपकीचकः ।\nहन्यतां शीघ्रमसती यत्कृते कीचको हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the gathered charioteers, Upakichaka said: \"Kill at once this unchaste woman, on whose account Kichaka was killed.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"अथ वा नेह हन्तव्या दह्यतां कामिना सह ।\nमृतस्यापि प्रियं कार्यं सूतपुत्रस्य सर्वथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Or rather, do not kill her here; let her be burned with her lover; for we must in every way do what pleases the dead charioteer's son.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो विराटमूचुस्ते कीचकोऽस्याः कृते हतः ।\nसहाद्यानेन दह्येत तदनुज्ञातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they said to Virata: \"Kichaka was killed because of her; she should be burned with him; you ought to permit it.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"पराक्रमं तु सूतानां मत्वा राजान्वमोदत ।\nसैरन्ध्र्याः सूतपुत्रेण सह दाहं विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, considering the might of the charioteers, agreed that the sairandhri should be burned with the charioteer's son, lord of the people."}},{"n":9,"text":"तां समासाद्य वित्रस्तां कृष्णां कमललोचनाम् ।\nमोमुह्यमानां ते तत्र जगृहुः कीचका भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming upon Krishna, the lotus-eyed woman, terrified and fainting, the Kichakas seized her roughly."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततस्तु तां समारोप्य निबध्य च सुमध्यमाम् ।\nजग्मुरुद्यम्य ते सर्वे श्मशानमभितस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they put the slender-waisted woman on the bier and bound her, and all lifted it and went toward the cremation ground."}},{"n":11,"text":"ह्रियमाणा तु सा राजन्सूतपुत्रैरनिन्दिता ।\nप्राक्रोशन्नाथमिच्छन्ती कृष्णा नाथवती सती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Carried off by the charioteer's sons, blameless Krishna cried out, seeking a protector though she had protectors, O king."}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"जयो जयन्तो विजयो जयत्सेनो जयद्बलः ।\nते मे वाचं विजानन्तु सूतपुत्रा नयन्ति माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jaya, Jayanta, Vijaya, Jayatsena, Jayadbala: may they hear my words; the charioteer's sons are carrying me off."}},{"n":13,"text":"येषां ज्यातलनिर्घोषो विस्फूर्जितमिवाशनेः ।\nव्यश्रूयत महायुद्धे भीमघोषस्तरस्विनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose bowstring's twang, like a thunderbolt's crash, was heard in the great battle, the fearsome roar of the swift ones,"}},{"n":14,"text":"रथघोषश्च बलवान्गन्धर्वाणां यशस्विनाम् ।\nते मे वाचं विजानन्तु सूतपुत्रा नयन्ति माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the mighty rumble of the glorious gandharvas' chariots: may they hear my words; the charioteer's sons are carrying me off."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्यास्ताः कृपणा वाचः कृष्णायाः परिदेविताः ।\nश्रुत्वैवाभ्यपतद्भीमः शयनादविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those pitiful lamenting words of Krishna, Bhima sprang from his bed without a thought."}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"अहं शृणोमि ते वाचं त्वया सैरन्ध्रि भाषिताम् ।\nतस्मात्ते सूतपुत्रेभ्यो न भयं भीरु विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I hear your words, sairandhri; therefore, timid lady, you have nothing to fear from the charioteer's sons."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा स महाबाहुर्विजजृम्भे जिघांसया ।\nततः स व्यायतं कृत्वा वेषं विपरिवर्त्य च ।\nअद्वारेणाभ्यवस्कन्द्य निर्जगाम बहिस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the mighty-armed man stretched himself, eager to kill; then he changed his dress and appearance, leaped over the wall by no door, and went out."}},{"n":18,"text":"स भीमसेनः प्राकारादारुज्य तरसा द्रुमम् ।\nश्मशानाभिमुखः प्रायाद्यत्र ते कीचका गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena tore a tree up with force from the rampart and set off toward the cremation ground, where the Kichakas had gone."}},{"n":19,"text":"स तं वृक्षं दशव्यामं सस्कन्धविटपं बली ।\nप्रगृह्याभ्यद्रवत्सूतान्दण्डपाणिरिवान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That strong man took that tree, ten fathoms tall with its trunk and branches, and rushed at the charioteers like Death with his staff."}},{"n":20,"text":"ऊरुवेगेन तस्याथ न्यग्रोधाश्वत्थकिंशुकाः ।\nभूमौ निपतिता वृक्षाः संघशस्तत्र शेरते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the force of his thighs, banyan, ashvattha and kimshuka trees fell to the ground and lay there in heaps."}},{"n":21,"text":"तं सिंहमिव संक्रुद्धं दृष्ट्वा गन्धर्वमागतम् ।\nवित्रेसुः सर्वतः सूता विषादभयकम्पिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the gandharva come like an enraged lion, the charioteers on every side trembled with dismay and fear."}},{"n":22,"text":"तमन्तकमिवायान्तं गन्धर्वं प्रेक्ष्य ते तदा ।\nदिधक्षन्तस्तदा ज्येष्ठं भ्रातरं ह्युपकीचकाः ।\nपरस्परमथोचुस्ते विषादभयकम्पिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the gandharva approach like Death, and wishing to burn their eldest brother, the Upakichakas said to one another, shaking with dismay and fear:"}},{"n":23,"text":"गन्धर्वो बलवानेति क्रुद्ध उद्यम्य पादपम् ।\nसैरन्ध्री मुच्यतां शीघ्रं महन्नो भयमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A mighty gandharva comes in anger, lifting a tree; let the sairandhri be freed quickly, for a great danger has come upon us.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"ते तु दृष्ट्वा तमाविद्धं भीमसेनेन पादपम् ।\nविमुच्य द्रौपदीं तत्र प्राद्रवन्नगरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bhimasena brandish the tree, they let go of Draupadi and ran toward the city."}},{"n":25,"text":"द्रवतस्तांस्तु संप्रेक्ष्य स वज्री दानवानिव ।\nशतं पञ्चाधिकं भीमः प्राहिणोद्यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them flee, Bhima, like the wielder of the thunderbolt against the danavas, sent a hundred and five of them to Yama's abode."}},{"n":26,"text":"तत आश्वासयत्कृष्णां प्रविमुच्य विशां पते ।\nउवाच च महाबाहुः पाञ्चालीं तत्र द्रौपदीम् ।\nअश्रुपूर्णमुखीं दीनां दुर्धर्षः स वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, releasing Krishna, he comforted her, O lord of men; and the mighty-armed, unassailable Vrikodara spoke to Panchali Draupadi, her face wet with tears and wretched."}},{"n":27,"text":"एवं ते भीरु वध्यन्ते ये त्वां क्लिश्यन्त्यनागसम् ।\nप्रैहि त्वं नगरं कृष्णे न भयं विद्यते तव ।\nअन्येनाहं गमिष्यामि विराटस्य महानसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is how those who torment you without cause, timid lady, are killed. Go to the city, Krishna; you have nothing to fear. I shall go to Virata's kitchen by another way.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"पञ्चाधिकं शतं तच्च निहतं तत्र भारत ।\nमहावनमिव छिन्नं शिश्ये विगलितद्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hundred and five lay killed there, Bharata, like a great forest felled, with trees tumbled."}},{"n":29,"text":"एवं ते निहता राजञ्शतं पञ्च च कीचकाः ।\nस च सेनापतिः पूर्वमित्येतत्सूतषट्शतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus a hundred and five Kichakas were killed, king, and that commander before them; in all one hundred and six charioteers."}},{"n":30,"text":"तद्दृष्ट्वा महदाश्चर्यं नरा नार्यश्च संगताः ।\nविस्मयं परमं गत्वा नोचुः किंचन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that great marvel, the men and women gathered there were utterly astonished and said nothing, Bharata."}}]}]}